From 1e43474115be13922e6769152011118bf7f75938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Mager <mikemager@codeaurora.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2014 14:53:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] M8: QCamera2: add "hal-buf-queue-size" parameter

With an infinite queue size, it was observed that as the device is
thermally mitigated and CPU clocks drop, the ability to empty the
queue falls drastically, eventually resulting in a crash due to too
many open file handles.

When the "hal-buf-queue-size" parameter is set to 1, the queue only
ever holds the most recently queued frame. This addresses the
problem described above, but has an additional benefit for the
augmented reality use case since the pose should always be
determined from the most recent frame.

Change-Id: I649462f8aa0981c6983cdb0d12833fdd89a8d0f6
---
 QCamera2/HAL/QCamera2HWI.h            |  3 +-
 QCamera2/HAL/QCamera2HWICallbacks.cpp | 35 +++++++++++++++++++--
 QCamera2/HAL/QCameraParameters.cpp    | 59 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 QCamera2/HAL/QCameraParameters.h      |  6 ++++
 4 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 mode change 100755 => 100644 QCamera2/HAL/QCameraParameters.cpp

